{"id": "EUVD-2026-102954", "enisaUuid": "1e2a9dbe-c759-3e2f-912b-a0c2557ea61c", "description": "Chaskiq through 2.0.3 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to fetch arbitrary URLs via the createUrlUpload GraphQL mutation. Attackers can submit internal URLs, including cloud instance metadata endpoints, through POST /graphql and retrieve the full response via the returned ActiveStorage blob URL.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:39:26", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/chaskiq-unauthenticated-ssrf-oembed-url-upload", "https://github.com/chaskiq/chaskiq/blob/2.0.3/app/graphql/mutations/create_url_upload.rb#L29-L66", "https://github.com/chaskiq/chaskiq/blob/2.0.3/app/controllers/graphql_controller.rb#L3-L33", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/chaskiq-through-2.0.3-ssrf-via-createurlupload-graphql-mutation"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rggr-4j68-hc5w", "CVE-2026-111663"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1abff121-bdd8-3d80-865e-c0c9dbe32c86", "product": {"name": "Chaskiq", "vendor": {"name": "chaskiq"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "22a416a7-2cb7-3ee2-ab3e-92ae44cf0cab", "vendor": {"name": "chaskiq"}}], "isExploited": false}